# Exercises continuous multi-call type feedback (VM::record_call_feedback /
# combined_param_feedback), not just the one-shot single-call sample it
# replaced as the compile-time speculation source.
#
# p(a, b) is called MANY times before its call_threshold is reached.
# Argument `a` is numeric on every single call. Argument `b` is numeric
# on every call EXCEPT one, right in the middle of warm-up, where it's a
# string. A one-shot sample taken from whichever call happens to trip
# the threshold might get lucky and never see that string call, wrongly
# speculating `b` as always-numeric; which would still be CORRECT
# (the entry guard re-validates for real either way) but would mean the
# accumulator isn't doing anything. Confirmed via ZURI_JIT_LOG=1 that
# `p` compiles with speculative_params=0x1 (bit 0 for `a` survives, bit
# 1 for `b` is correctly and permanently excluded by the one string
# call), never 0x3; proving the AND-accumulation is actually driving
# the decision, not just along for the ride. Large iteration count is
# deliberate: gives the background compiler thread enough wall-clock
# room to finish and get drained/logged before the (otherwise very
# fast) loop exits.
def p(a, b) {
  if is_number(b) {
    return a + b
  }
  return a + 1000
}

var total = 0
var i = 0
while i < 200000 {
  if i == 137 {
    total = total + p(i, "not-a-number")
  } else {
    total = total + p(i, i * 2)
  }
  i = i + 1
}
echo total
